WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.780
It is so decided...

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:11.870
Visible relief after two weeks of intense
negotiations produced a compromise in Katowice

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:17.270
With approximately 200 countries in the room,
it is not easy to find agreement on a deal

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.289
so specific and so technical.

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:27.010
Under these circumstances, every single step
forward is a big achievement

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:33.100
The deal sets out rules to implement and finance
the 2015 Paris climate agreement - which aims

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:39.440
to limit global temperature increases to below
two degrees Celsius.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.429
This generation has the responsibility to
show how we keep our planet livable, how we

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:47.039
can make sure that we reduce CO2.

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:48.399
And here we showed the way.

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:50.229
That's important."

00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:54.049
But alongside the backslapping there was also
criticism.

00:00:54.049 --> 00:00:59.279
Activists were hoping for more ambitious climate
goals - after scientists recently warned that

00:00:59.279 --> 00:01:05.390
a cap of 1.5 degrees celcius and a radical
shift away from fossil fuels are needed to

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:06.670
avert disaster.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.430
I think certainly the fossil fuel countries
here slowed things down.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:18.320
I think that the United States certainly did
not help on the issue of having science move

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.320
forward.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.149
But there was just an overall lack of leadership
from the European Union, as well on getting

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:27.000
ambition out of the agreement."

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.890
15-year-old Swede Greta Thunberg has become
a voice for the younger generation by inspiring

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:37.490
children all over the world to strike from
school in protest at climate change.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:40.950
She had sharp words for the adults at the
conference.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:46.899
You say you love your children above all else
and yet you`re stealing their future in front

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:50.880
of their very eyes.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:57.259
Until you start focusing on what needs to
be done rather than what is politically possible

00:01:57.259 --> 00:02:01.229
there is no hope.

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:06.859
Climate activists - both young and old - feel
world leaders have once again done too little,

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.349
too late.

00:02:08.349 --> 00:02:10.580
SHUT IT DOWN!!

